# RSX - Manage resident extensions

```text
RSX LIST
RSX LOAD [DU:]name
RSX UNLOAD name
```

## Select a terminal

RSX LIST identifies loaded extensions. If ADM3A is active and you want
ANSI, replace the personality before starting the application.

```text
RSX UNLOAD ADM3A
RSX LOAD ANSI
HELP PIP
```

HELP discovers the active personality. For an ADM3A screen test, load
ADM3A and run [ADMTST](ADMTST.HLP).

## Other services

```text
RSX LOAD NDR
NDR
STAT MEM
```

The first command installs the named-directory provider. A program can
return to CP/M while the provider stays loaded. [STAT](STAT.HLP) shows
available transient memory. Save wanted [NDR](NDR.HLP) assignments
before unloading NDR.
